{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/793425-beasts-and-changelings","id":793425,"title":"Beasts and Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-26T22:01:18-08:00","id":793425,"title":"Beasts and Changelings","content":"Is it possible that a Changeling would ally with a Beast for protection? Like the Beast protects the Changeling from the True Fae and the Fae's servants that are hunting him and in return the Changeling serves the Beast either by performing certain tasks or spying for the Beast.<br /> <br /> I am just curious because originally I was planning on doing a Changeling campaign but after finding out about Beasts I was really wanting to do a Beast campaign. However my brother had already created a changeling character and I was trying to think of a way his changeling could work with other beast characters.<br /> <br /> Plus they did say that Beasts could easily cross over with other races in NWoD.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any constructive feedback on this feel free to mention it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":7343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","user":"Werescythe","date":".  added stuff. 12-27-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T22:27:33-08:00","id":793435,"title":"","content":"On concept I see no reason it couldn't happen. I mean Beast's need to have Changeling they consider kin in order to be able to learn those kinship nightmares, so mechanically there's incentive to a Beast and Changeling associating. Heck pg 59 in the book says as far as many Beasts are concerned Changelings might as well be Beasts and that the Fair Folk weird out the Beasts as well.<br /> <br /> You'll probably need to figure out the type of Beast you have running since the why might change. I mean are they helping the Changeling out from a sense of altruism, because they like the Changeling, they dislike the Fair Folk, the Beast is territorial? Is it figuring the Changeling will help with feeding its Horror; if so how? A tyrant might very well just enjoy having the Changeling become a subordinate, or be able to feed off any situation where they show off superiority by repelling the servants of the Fae. A collector might view the Changeling as a means to feed its desire for certain objects if it doesn't just think the Changeling should be part of its collection. Those sort of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:21:30-08:00","id":793760,"title":"","content":"Another bonus in favor of a Beast/Changeling alliance is that Family Dinner means that a Changeling provides an alternate source of Satiety for a Beast - it just needs to be nearby when the Changeling draws Glamor from people (well, so long as it was a hunt of sorts). Likewise, Beasts change the Hedge when they go through it like a high-Wyrd Changeling, or one of the True Fae, so there's a bit of status that can come from that. The fact they both deal with dreams, too, means that they have some synergy there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:40:38-08:00","id":793840,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Beast/Changeling game right now, and there are plenty of good reasons to team up. The Autumn Court in particular is very Beast friendly, being as interested in the wider occult world and fear as they are. There's a ravager associated with the Dawn Court, when something needs to be destroyed so that new things can be built in its place, he's their man. There's a tyrant in Summer who gets his power fix beating down minions of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, Beasts bring a lot of raw power to the table. They're a rather combat oriented splat and Changelings benefit from having a big brother figure around when the huntsmen come calling. Particularly in dreamspace, a Beast's Horror is vastly more powerful than the average character, which can give Changelings an edge. Risky for the Beast, but worth noting.<br /> <br /> However, Changelings have a lot more in the way of finesse and subtle tricks than the average Beast. They can observe dreams without turning them into nightmares, maybe even craft a soothing fantasy. They also feed a lot more lightly, which a Beast can benefit from by proxy. <br /> <br /> It definitely has the potential to be a good symbiotic relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T17:41:07-08:00","id":793861,"title":"","content":"I am definitely glad to see that it can work very well. My thought was that perhaps the changeling players would escape from their True Fae masters and while being chased by the True Fae's servants would be saved by the Beast players before becoming allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T20:59:58-08:00","id":793929,"title":"","content":"I have this image in my head of a Beast acting as a relationship counselor between a changeling and his/her former keeper because he wants to help both members of his &quot;family&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}